course: dictionary
lesson: 12820
title: Embryo: the very early stage
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An embryo is a living thing at a very early stage of growing, before it is born or hatches. «Inside the egg, the chick embryo grew a little more each day.» The clues are egg and grew: the embryo is the tiny young chick, not yet hatched.
explain: Embryos grow in different places: inside an egg, inside a seed, or inside a mother's womb. «Each bean seed holds a tiny embryo that will grow into a new plant.» Here the seed is the place, and the embryo is the part that will become a plant.
explain: Embryo has another meaning too. When something is «in embryo», it is at a very early stage and may develop later. «Our club idea is still in embryo.» The words still and may tell you it has only just started, like an idea that is not yet finished.
fact: An embryo is a living thing at a very early stage of growing.
fact: A chick embryo grows inside an egg, and a human embryo grows in the womb.
fact: The tiny part inside a seed that will grow into a new plant is also called an embryo.
fact: «In embryo» means at a very early stage, like «a plan in embryo», which has only just started.
exercise: «Inside the egg, the chick embryo grew a little more each day.» What is an embryo here? | A nest made of straw | A cracked shell left after hatching | *A living thing at a very early stage of growing | A type of hen
exercise: «Each bean seed holds a tiny embryo that will grow into a new plant.» Where is the embryo in a bean seed? | On the leaf | *Inside the seed | In the pod | In the soil
exercise: «Our club idea is still in embryo, so it may grow later.» What does in embryo suggest? | Finished and ready to use | *At a very early stage that may develop later | Very large | Lost forever
test: «The mother bird sat on the eggs, keeping each embryo warm.» What is each embryo? | A grown-up bird | A kind of nest | A broken shell | *A living thing at an early stage of growing
test: Where does a human embryo grow before it is born? | Inside a seed | In the sea | *In the womb | On a hill
exam: What does embryo mean in «Ava's invention is still in embryo»? | Broken and thrown away | Made of glass | Finished and sold in shops | *At a very early stage, not yet fully formed
